1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,854
What actually happens when you crack your knuckles?

2
00:00:03,114 --> 00:00:04,645
It's not your bones popping.

3
00:00:04,905 --> 00:00:09,482
Stretch the joint, and the fluid inside instantly forms a gas cavity.

4
00:00:09,742 --> 00:00:13,862
In 2015, scientists caught it live on an MRI.

5
00:00:14,122 --> 00:00:17,134
The pop is the bubble being born, not bursting.

6
00:00:17,394 --> 00:00:20,821
That's why you can't crack the same knuckle for about twenty minutes.

7
00:00:21,081 --> 00:00:22,582
So does it wreck your joints?

8
00:00:22,842 --> 00:00:25,914
Researchers followed habitual crackers for years.

9
00:00:26,174 --> 00:00:28,248
No link to arthritis. None.

10
00:00:28,508 --> 00:00:30,584
The sound is physics, not damage.

11
00:00:30,844 --> 00:00:32,540
Now you can un-hear the myth.
